   342	## Phase 3 — change-impact verification (sealed backend)
   343	Use only sealed `manifest.phase3Backend` to select the verifier path. When it is `workflow`,
   344	immediately before fan-out refresh mdq whenever `MDQ_AVAILABLE` is true: re-run the same
   345	two-part preflight as Phase 0 — first
   346	`bash "$SD/scripts/mdq-index.sh" --config "$CFG" --repo-root "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"`, re-parse
   347	its JSON, and re-bind `MDQ_AVAILABLE`/`MDQ_BIN`; then, if it is still available, run
   348	`(cd "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" && python3 "$SD/scripts/mdq-health.py" --bin "<MDQ_BIN>")` and
   349	re-bind `MDQ_HEALTHY`/`MDQ_CHUNKS`/`MDQ_STATUS`. If either refresh step fails, or the health
   350	probe is unhealthy, re-bind `MDQ_AVAILABLE=false` when indexing is unavailable and always bind
   351	`MDQ_HEALTHY=false`; use mdq in fan-out only when both values are true, otherwise use
   352	grep-degrade. Bind the refresh failure detail for the Phase-5 mdq status line. Phase 0
   353	establishes the initial index; this repeat is the freshness guarantee immediately before fan-out.
   354	When sealed `phase3Backend` is `codex`, skip this refresh: the dispatcher deliberately never uses
   355	mdq and supplies grep-degrade instructions to every Codex process.
   356	
   357	Seal the run immediately after the applicable mdq refresh (or immediately for `codex`) and before
   358	any verifier starts:
   359	`python3 "$SD/scripts/seal-run.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --repo-root "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" --evidence "$EVIDENCE"`.
   360	On success replace `EVIDENCE` with its complete stdout; its `digest` and updated `manifest` are
   361	the trusted seal. Exit 5 means the HEAD or complete change set drifted after Phase 1: release the
   362	run, stop, and say “Phase 1 以降にソースが変わりました。監査を再実行してください。” Do
   363	not launch either verifier backend and do not calculate a replacement digest by hand.
   364	
   365	If `DISPATCH[]` is empty, do not launch either backend. Send the literal empty array `[]` to
   366	`python3 "$SD/scripts/write-evidence.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --name returns --stdin --evidence "$EVIDENCE"`
   367	and replace `EVIDENCE` with stdout; `returns` must always be a real evidence file and can never use
   368	the `none` sentinel.
   369	
   370	If `DISPATCH[]` is non-empty and sealed `phase3Backend` is `codex`, select
   371	`PHASE3_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna` for `RUN_CLASS=light` or
   372	`PHASE3_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra` for `RUN_CLASS=standard`, then run:
   373	`python3 "$SD/scripts/codex-dispatch.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --repo-root "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" --model "$PHASE3_CODEX_MODEL" --effort medium --timeout-seconds <sealed manifest.phase3CodexTimeoutSeconds> --concurrency 4`.
   374	Parse and report its stdout summary `returnsPath`/`attempts`/`ok`/`failed`. The dispatcher performs
   375	up to three cumulative attempts, preserves every failed assignment as a null return row, and
   376	publishes only validated verdicts. Send its complete `$RUN_DIR/returns.json` through
   377	`python3 "$SD/scripts/write-evidence.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --name returns --stdin --evidence "$EVIDENCE" < "$RUN_DIR/returns.json"`
   378	and replace `EVIDENCE` with stdout. Then run
   379	`python3 "$SD/scripts/check-verdicts.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --impact-json "$RUN_DIR/impact.json" --returns`
   380	and retain the final `missing`, `returnMissing`, `mismatch`, `invalid`, `duplicates`, and
   381	`manifestMismatch` arrays for the report. Do not launch Workflow or perform an orchestrator retry
   382	on this path; the dispatcher already owns all three attempts.
   383	
   384	Codex absence, failed authentication, launch failure, non-zero exit, timeout, or invalid output is
   385	fail-closed. Never silently fall back to Workflow: the dispatcher retains null rows, retries to its
   386	limit, and the gate then REFUSES incomplete evidence. Tell the user to repair/install/authenticate
   387	Codex, or set `phase3Backend` back to `workflow` and rerun the audit.
   388	
   389	If `DISPATCH[]` is non-empty and sealed `phase3Backend` is `workflow`, launch
   390	`Workflow({scriptPath: "$SD/references/workflow-template.js", args: {repoRoot: CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, changeSummary, impacted: DISPATCH entries with provenance, verifierModel: RUN_CLASS == "light" ? "haiku" : "sonnet", mdqAvailable: MDQ_AVAILABLE, mdqHealthy: MDQ_HEALTHY, cmAvailable: CM_AVAILABLE, axAvailable: AX_AVAILABLE, symbolGraphAvailable: SYMBOL_GRAPH_AVAILABLE, runId: RUNID, runDir: RUN_DIR, scriptsDir: "$SD/scripts"}})`.
   391	Pass dispatch entries only — never cached paths. The template preserves two runtime-dependent
   392	facts: Workflow `args` may arrive as a JSON string, and `agentType` is always plugin-namespaced
   393	(`docaudit:doc-impact-verifier-light` for Haiku or `docaudit:doc-impact-verifier` for Sonnet),
   394	never a bare name and never selected through `opts.model` precedence.
   395	`runId`/`runDir`/`scriptsDir` are REQUIRED. Each verifier first persists its own runid-stamped
   396	verdict via the supplied `write-verdict.py --run-dir ... --out ... --runid ... --path ...
   397	--verdict ...` command (`--source` is omitted, so it is a verifier record), then returns a
   398	structured verdict. Do not write verifier files from the orchestrator.
   399	
   400	For Workflow attempt 1, add `attempt:1` to every template return and append the whole returned array to an
   401	in-memory cumulative returns array. The template itself always emits one element per assignment:
   402	`{assignedPath,returnedPath,verdict,rationale,suggestion}`, normalizing both a null agent return and
   403	a null slot returned by `parallel()` to null fields. Therefore, when Workflow returns an array,
   404	element omission cannot occur. If Workflow throws before it can return an array at all, represent
   405	every assignment from that attempt with the same `assignedPath` and null return fields so the failed
   406	attempt remains explicit.
   407	Write the complete cumulative array (replace, never append the file) through
   408	`python3 "$SD/scripts/write-evidence.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --name returns --stdin --evidence "$EVIDENCE"`
   409	and replace `EVIDENCE` with stdout. Then run
   410	`python3 "$SD/scripts/check-verdicts.py" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" --impact-json "$RUN_DIR/impact.json" --returns`
   411	and parse `missing`, `returnMissing`, `mismatch`, `invalid`, `duplicates`, and
   412	`manifestMismatch`. `returns.json` is mandatory gate evidence, not progress-only display.
   413	
   414	On the Workflow path, re-dispatch the union `missing ∪ returnMissing ∪ mismatch`, preserving provenance, at most twice
   415	after the initial attempt. Attempts 2 and 3 ALWAYS set `verifierModel:"sonnet"`, including retries
   416	after partial nulls or a Workflow throw. After each attempt, add its attempt number, rewrite the
   417	complete cumulative returns array through `write-evidence.py`, replace `EVIDENCE`, and rerun
   418	`check-verdicts.py --returns`. The sealed digest is assumed unchanged and will be rechecked by the
   419	gate; do not use the retired ad-hoc tree-digest calculation. If an exceptional retry decision
   420	needs an early confirmation, call `tree-digest.py --repo-root "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"
   421	--include-head` with one `--exclude` for every exact `manifest.digestExclude[]` entry and require
   422	the result to equal `EVIDENCE.digest`. Never broaden those excludes. After three total attempts,
   423	continue to Phase 4 with incomplete evidence so the deterministic gate can REFUSE it. The Codex
   424	path likewise continues after its final checker result. Record the final checker arrays for the
   425	report. (Built-in `/code-review` and `/security-review` cannot run
   426	inside Workflow; they remain in Phase 4.)
   427	
   428	## Phase 4 — existing layers + reviews (main loop, sequential)
   429	Global gate: run this phase's delegated checks **iff** sealed `manifest.json` has
   430	`phase4Required:true`. Do not re-derive this decision from impacted/SSOT/mode in the orchestrator.
   431	1. From config `docAuditCommands`, run `existence` then `semantic` then `format`
   432	   (e.g. `/check-docs`, `doc-lint`, `/review-docs`) — whole-tree (no per-file arg).
   433	   Invoke each exactly as the config value names it (a skill like `doc-lint` is
   434	   invoked by name, not with a leading slash). A command classified `invalid` by Phase 0.5 is never
   435	   invoked here either; retain its pre-flight FAIL finding and run the built-in generic layer for
   436	   that layer instead, using the same fallback as an unavailable command. **Fallback:** if `docAuditCommands`
   437	   is absent, or a given layer's command is unavailable in this environment, run the
   438	   built-in generic layer instead:
   439	   `python3 "$SD/scripts/generic-layers.py" --layer <format|existence|semantic> --config "$CFG" --repo-root "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"`
   440	   (in incremental mode you may add `--paths -` and pipe the impacted-doc list to scope it;
   441	   the semantic layer always scans the full repo for orphan-reference resolution regardless).
   442	   Fold its `findings[]` into the verdict: `severity:"FAIL"` -> NEEDS FIX, `severity:"WARN"` -> report only.
   443	   For the stamped `doc-lint` template in `installed`, and any adjusted command whose adjustment
   444	   explicitly adopted that contract, parse strict `path:line - FAIL|WARN - message` finding lines and
   445	   fold those severities. For every other model-driven delegated command, fold every reported finding
   446	   regardless of layout, normalizing `FAIL`/`HIGH`/`CRITICAL` to blocking and `WARN`/`MEDIUM`/`LOW`/`INFO`
   447	   to non-blocking. A final `VERDICT` line, when present, is a consistency check only; missing,
   448	   ambiguous, or contradictory output adds a non-blocking WARN and `parsed:false`.
   449	2. If `boundaryCommand` set and gate open, run it.
   450	3. Handle `reviewCommands.code` (e.g. `/code-review high`) on the working diff, then
   451	   `reviewCommands.security` (e.g. `/security-review`). Normalize any
   452	   `/security-audit ...` request to `/security-review`. In an interactive session,
